<p>
  Your <%= link_to "#{render_money @ledger_item.amount_cents.abs} charge", ledger_item_url(@ledger_item) %> on <%= @ledger_item.datetime.strftime("%B #{@ledger_item.datetime.day.ordinalize}") %> was reversed by <strong><%= @merchant_name %></strong>. Your balance has been updated to reflect this reversal.
</p>

<h3 class="mb-2">Wasn't expecting this reversal?</h3>
<p class="my-0">
  Merchants like <strong><%= @merchant_name %></strong> often reverse charges when an order is canceled or a refund is requested, but a very common cause is their fraud detection flagging the purchase, often because your billing information doesn't match what's on file &mdash; or for another reason at their sole discretion. To find out why this charge was reversed, we recommend reaching out to <%= @merchant_name %> directly.
</p>

<% if @failed_verification_checks.present? %>
  <h3 class="mb-2">Troubleshooting tips</h3>
  <p class="my-0">
    <% if @failed_verification_checks.include?("address_postal_code_check") %>
      We noticed that the zip code used at <%= @merchant_name %> didn't match the billing zip code on your <%= link_to "HCB card", stripe_card_url(@card_charge.stripe_card) %> (<%= @card_charge.stripe_cardholder.address_postal_code %>). Please try again using that zip code.
    <% elsif @failed_verification_checks.include?("address_line1_check") %>
      We noticed that the billing address used at <%= @merchant_name %> didn't match the billing address on your <%= link_to "HCB card", stripe_card_url(@card_charge.stripe_card) %>. Please try again using your HCB billing address.
    <% elsif @failed_verification_checks.include?("cvc_check") %>
      We noticed that the CVC used at <%= @merchant_name %> didn't match your <%= link_to "HCB card", stripe_card_url(@card_charge.stripe_card) %>. Please try again with the correct CVC.
    <% end %>
  </p>
<% end %>

<p>
  <%= link_to "Click here to view this transaction.", ledger_item_url(@ledger_item) %>
</p>